      <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0087-7166">ORCID</a>
      <span class="sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Sarah-Barns-4">ResearchGate</a>
      <span class="sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=cnGxyWQAAAAJ&amp;hl=en">Google Scholar</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">My favourite personal work</h2>
    <div class="pub-item">
      <div class="pub-title"><a href="https://www.studioesem.com/projects/superorganism">Superorganism: Listening to the Anthropocene</a></div>
      <div class="pub-details">Creative Director &amp; Lead Sound Designer, 2022</div>
      <span class="pub-tag">Sound &amp; installation</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Previous positions</h2>
    <p class="prev-roles">
      Before RMIT I held an Industry Fellowship at the QUT Design Lab and a Visiting Fellowship at the
      Melbourne Centre for Cities (2021&ndash;22), and before that was Engaged Research Fellow
      (2018&ndash;19) and Urban Studies Foundation Postdoctoral Research Fellow (2014&ndash;17) at the
      Institute for Culture and Society, Western Sydney University. From 2015 to 2017 I was Future
      Cities Advisor at CSIRO&rsquo;s Data61, on secondment from Western Sydney University, leading
      strategic advisory work on smart cities, data governance and urban living labs.
    </p>
    <p class="prev-roles">
      I co-directed Esem Projects from 2013 to 2022 and ran Sitelines Media Research Consulting from
      2019 to 2022. Earlier roles include Digital and Organisational Strategy Lead at the ABC
      (2011&ndash;12), Senior Consultant in Urban Informatics at Arup (2011&ndash;13), and Manager of
      Strategic Initiatives at the UTS Creative Industries Innovation Centre (2008&ndash;11). My career
      began in public policy in 2000, with roles across the Department of Communications, the media
      and telecommunications think-tank Network Insight, the Australian Communications and Media
      Authority, the Australia Council for the Arts and the ABC.
    </p>
    <div class="honour">
      <span class="honour-year">2005&ndash;2010</span>
      <span class="honour-body">
        <span class="honour-name">Doctor of Philosophy</span>
        <span class="honour-detail">University of Technology Sydney</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="honour">
      <span class="honour-year">1993&ndash;1998</span>
      <span class="honour-body">
        <span class="honour-name">Bachelor of Arts (First Class Honours), Politics &amp; International Relations</span>
        <span class="honour-detail">Murdoch University</span>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
